<title>NETHERLANDS: ABN AMRO buys 74 pct of Poland's Maklerski.</title>
<headline>ABN AMRO buys 74 pct of Poland's Maklerski.</headline>
<dateline>AMSTERDAM 1996-09-19</dateline>
<text>
<p>Dutch bank ABN AMRO NV said on Thursday it had bought 74 percent of Polish securities house Dom Maklerski.  </p>
<p>&quot;The acquisition is in line with ABN AMRO's strategy to build up a fully working investment bank,&quot; ABN AMRO said.</p>
<p>The Polish firm has 28 employees and deals with private investors.</p>
<p>The price of the acquisition was not disclosed.</p>
<p>ABN AMRO has 1,670 offices in 68 countries worldwide.</p>
<p>-- Amsterdam newsroom +31 20 504 5000 fax +31 20 504 5040</p>
</text>
